        "layout": {
          "pady": 4,
          "sticky": "nsew"
        },
        "fields": {
          "notes": {
            "type": "_TextInput",
            "label": {
              "En": "Notes",
              "Fr": "Notes",
              "De": "Notes",
              "Es": "Notes"
            },
            "value_default": "---",
            "device_state": "notes",
            "read_only": true,
            "layout": {
              "width": "100%",
              "font": 13
            }
          },
          "raw_idn": {
            "type": "_TextInput",
            "label": {
              "En": "*IDN? reply",
              "Fr": "*IDN? reply",
              "De": "*IDN? reply",
              "Es": "*IDN? reply"
            },
            "value_default": "---",
            "device_state": "raw_idn",
            "read_only": true,
            "layout": {
              "width": "100%",
              "font": 13
            }
          }
        },
        "notes": "READ-ONLY ON PURPOSE, AND SAYS SO. Every model in this class declares \"vocabulary\": \"none\" in its .gui sheet and carries no .komand table, so there is no command for a control here to name, and rightly: a knob that cannot reach an instrument is worse than no knob. Nothing would catch one — the old `check.sh binding` lane that refused it is retired, and `prune_unbindable` (NODE.BareMetal ORCHESTRATOR:hunter:VISA) prunes nothing for a model with no .komand table — so this note is the rule. bind_state is what a console for a device it cannot drive is for. Authoring <Model>.komand beside <Model>.gui is what adds controls."
      }
    }
